  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The square of an integer is called a perfect square. If \\(x\\) is a perfect square, the next larger perfect square is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x+1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x^2+1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(x^2+2x+1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(x^2+x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(x+2\\sqrt x+1\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1979-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(x=n^2\\) with \\(n\\ge0.\\) The next larger perfect square is \\[ \\begin{aligned} (n+1)^2&=n^2+2n+1\\\\ &=x+2\\sqrt x+1. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(x=n^2\\) for a nonnegative integer \\(n\\)",
        "Expand the next square \\((n+1)^2\\) and replace \\(n\\) by \\(\\sqrt x\\)"
      ],
